MID_EV00_006_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_006_m01_001: This is it. Let's get to the surface and head\nfor Dagsion.
MID_EV00_006_m01_002: <NCA>"What is this place?"
MID_EV00_006_m01_003: I don't know much about it, but...I've heard it\nwas built thousands of years ago.
MID_EV00_006_m01_004: Most traces of civilization on the surface at the time\nof the Great Undoing have been wiped away.
MID_EV00_006_m01_005: But some of the facilities built underground survived\nand are still in operation.
MID_EV00_006_m01_006: <NCA>"It's incredible."
MID_EV00_006_m01_007: <NCB>"What did they do here?"
MID_EV00_006_m01_008: <ACA>To be honest, even I'm amazed at what they could do\nbefore the Great Undoing.
MID_EV00_006_m01_020: <ACA>It was built so the parts don't wear down. They\nbelieved it would be in use for 10 thousand years.
MID_EV00_006_m01_009: <ACB>I think it was once a facility to observe the sea\nof stars.
MID_EV00_006_m01_021: <ACB>Apparently there were lots of things like this in the\nworld that was.
MID_EV00_006_m01_011: Now, though...almost no one knows this place exists.
MID_EV00_006_m01_012: And the people of today could never build anything\nlike it.
MID_EV00_006_m01_013: I guess it's the way of things for a dead civilization\nto be forgotten and fade away.
MID_EV00_006_m01_014: Dagda the Great feared everything about the world\nthat was. He wanted all of this eliminated.
MID_EV00_006_m01_015: Thinking back, it's the whole reason the Battle of\nFezzan happened.
MID_EV00_006_m01_016: Hah...
MID_EV00_006_m01_017: <NCA>"Are you alright?"
MID_EV00_006_m01_018: Yes... I'm sorry. It's nothing, really.
MID_EV00_006_m01_019: I don't know what I was thinking, opening up to\nyou about all this.
MID_GM00_02_m01: <TH>
MID_GM00_02_m01_001: We should keep moving. Fortuna is waiting for us\nin Dagsion.
MID_EV00_008_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_008_m01_001: From here, Dagsion is a stone's throw away.
MID_EV00_008_m01_002: But I have no idea what it's like inside the city now.
MID_EV00_008_m01_003: With a gate of the underworld there, it's probably\ninfested with the risen dead.
MID_EV00_008_m01_004: All of them against the two of us...those aren't good\nodds, even with you.
MID_EV00_008_m01_005: <NCA>"We'll get through them."
MID_EV00_008_m01_006: <NCB>"That does sound dire."
MID_EV00_008_m01_007: <ACA>Heh. Why does you saying so make me feel like\nwe can handle it?
MID_EV00_008_m01_008: <ACA>You're a strange one.
MID_EV00_008_m01_009: <ACB>It...it doesn't matter. What else can we do?
MID_EV00_008_m01_039: <ACB>We just have to make a beeline for Fortuna's temple\nand join forces with her.
MID_EV00_008_m01_010: So you've finally come, Hong Hua. I was getting tired\nof waiting.
MID_EV00_008_m01_011: Troy! What are you doing here?!
MID_EV00_008_m01_012: Zenon got in contact with me a while ago and asked\nthat I help you out.
MID_EV00_008_m01_013: <NCA>"I'm not sure who you are."
MID_EV00_008_m01_014: <NCB>"Hong Hua, who is this?"
MID_EV00_008_m01_015: <ACA>Ah, right. We technically haven't met.
MID_EV00_008_m01_042: <ACB>
MID_EV00_008_m01_016: This is Troy. She's also from Nuwa, where she was\nsecond in command after Master Zenon.
MID_EV00_008_m01_017: That's why I'll be coming with you.
MID_EV00_008_m01_018: I must say, you turned out handsomely. Even at my\nage, I think I might be falling for you.
MID_EV00_008_m01_019: I must say, you turned out beautifully. Just like me\nwhen I was young.
MID_EV00_008_m01_040: Troy, I'm sorry to tell you this, but...Master Zenon\nwon't be coming back.
MID_EV00_008_m01_041: I know. I'm sure Zenon was very pleased with his\nfinal project.
MID_EV00_008_m01_029: Speaking of which...you've been given a sizable\ntask, haven't you?
MID_EV00_008_m01_030: Zenon told me. Saving the world is ambitious.
MID_EV00_008_m01_032: But I'm interested. So I'm here to help.
MID_EV00_009_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_009_m01_001: This is ridiculous. I can't believe Lind is here.
MID_EV00_009_m01_024: From Lord of Impalement to undead watchdog...\nHow the mighty have fallen.
MID_EV00_009_m01_002: I remember you... The woman who nipped at\nMagistra Raksha's heels like a lost puppy.
MID_EV00_009_m01_003: Didn't take long for you to switch loyalties after she\nkicked you to the curb.
MID_EV00_009_m01_004: You're just a stray dog, following any master who'll\nfeed you... Pathetic.
MID_EV00_009_m01_005: So the risen dead still have the power of speech.\nThen listen when I tell you to get out of my way.
MID_EV00_009_m01_006: We're not here for you. Leave, or this gets ugly.
MID_EV00_009_m01_007: By order of my lord Balor, no one can pass here.
MID_EV00_009_m01_008: Your foolishness will be exposed and your bodies\nscattered to the winds. Like the rest of these corpses.
MID_EV00_009_m01_009: But do not fear... Death is liberation.
MID_EV00_009_m01_013: You were a terror even when you were alive, but at\nleast then you had a certain charisma.
MID_EV00_009_m01_014: Bark, bark, dog. You, though...I don't know you.\nWho is this?
MID_EV00_009_m01_015: <NCA>Stare Lind down.
MID_EV00_009_m01_016: <NCB>"I'm no one."
MID_EV00_009_m01_017: <ACA>There's something about you that offends me to my\ncore...though I couldn't say why.
MID_EV00_009_m01_018: <ACB>You're kidding me. I look forward to sewing your\ndead lips shut.
MID_EV00_009_m01_019: That spear you carry is odd too...
MID_EV00_009_m01_020: It's on the tip of my brain... Are you...
MID_EV00_009_m01_021: No... I still can't place you. You seem determined\nto face me, though.
MID_EV00_009_m01_022: So I'll oblige you. When you die here, your body will\nbe added to my forest of corpses.
MID_EV00_009_m01_023: Souls I shall offer to my lord Balor.
MID_EV00_010_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_010_m01_001: Impossible... With the strength of the underworld,\nI should be undefeatable.
MID_EV00_010_m01_002: Who are you? You can't possibly be human...
MID_EV00_010_m01_003: *gasp* Ahaha...so you weren't as dead as we\nall thought.
MID_EV00_010_m01_004: Haha! Ha... What a funny joke! I didn't think things\nlike this happened in real life.
MID_EV00_010_m01_005: That said... I'm not beaten yet.
MID_EV00_010_m01_007: I bet you can guess who guards the underworld gate\nin Dagsion. You will never beat him.
MID_EV00_010_m01_009: Haha... Heh... May you all roam the depths of\ndespair together.
MID_EV00_010_m01_010: Balor adores the despair of the living... Do your best...\nto satisfy him.
MID_EV00_010_m01_014: That's enough out of you. Crawl back to your grave.
MID_EV00_010_m01_016: Hahaha! You'll be following me there soon enough.\nI'll see you in the underworld.
MID_EV00_010_m01_017: Hehehe... Hahahaha...
MID_EV00_010_m01_018: He was somehow even more of a terror in death than\nin life.
MID_EV00_010_m01_019: The living can never coexist with the dead. There's\nno point trying to reason with them.
MID_EV00_010_m01_020: Though his last words were unsettling. I wonder\nwhat he meant by them.
MID_EV00_011_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_011_m01_001: Troy...was all that really necessary?
MID_EV00_011_m01_002: That's the force it takes to get anything into the skull\nof a man like that.
MID_EV00_011_m01_003: It's good to see you again, Fortuna. That's another\none I owe you.
MID_EV00_011_m01_007: I came to welcome you, not to rescue you. How did\nyou get into such trouble already?
MID_EV00_011_m01_008: You shouldn't lower your guard like that. If not for\nme, you would have perished.
MID_EV00_011_m01_009: <NCA>"I'm sorry."
MID_EV00_011_m01_010: <NCB>"I knew you would come through."
MID_EV00_011_m01_011: <ACA>How refreshingly humble! There's hope for you yet.
MID_EV00_011_m01_012: <ACA>I must say, I vastly prefer this version of you to\nthe last. Hehehe.
MID_EV00_011_m01_013: <ACB>Hmph! That's only another way of saying you\nwon't stand up for yourself.
MID_EV00_011_m01_014: <ACB>I am not your bodyguard, and I'll thank you not to\npresume upon my protection.
MID_EV00_011_m01_015: Weren't you going to wait for us at your temple?
MID_EV00_011_m01_016: I was, but I had an inkling there might be trouble.\n'Tis a good thing I came.
MID_EV00_011_m01_017: I did prepare this while I waited, though. I hope\nyou're sufficiently grateful.
MID_EV00_011_m01_018: <NCA>"What is this?"
MID_EV00_011_m01_019: It looks like sand, but it's much more than that.\nMy power is imbued in it.
MID_EV00_011_m01_020: I shall name it...Divine Sand.
MID_EV00_011_m01_021: Use this, and even you can wield my—er, rather,\nthe power of the progenitor god.
MID_EV00_011_m01_022: As I just demonstrated, it can turn back time.
MID_EV00_011_m01_023: Keep it, for it may save your life in battle.
MID_EV00_011_m01_024: But use it wisely. My precious power is not to be\nwasted at every chance!
MID_EV00_011_m01_025: What's the next step, Fortuna? Should we destroy\nthe underworld gate in Dagsion?
MID_EV00_011_m01_026: A splendid idea...if you weren't such a meager crew.
MID_EV00_011_m01_027: We few have no hope against Balor's forces. Hmm.
MID_EV00_011_m01_028: If we had 10 times the troops we do now, 'twould\ngive us a fighting chance.
MID_EV00_011_m01_029: How can we find that many in this wasteland?
MID_EV00_011_m01_030: Ha! You can't! But there is a way nonetheless.\nI've laid out a path for you.
MID_EV00_011_m01_031: Did you think I was dozing the whole time?
MID_EV00_011_m01_032: Follow me, and I shall explain.